
                            Welcome to ApT-BBS!
                             V1.10 3-May-1997

To get started as soon as possible you should read either the APT-BBS! guide
or doc file FIRST. Then set-up your BBS configuration as explained in the
documentation.

The files mentioned above can be found in sub-directory [APT/Guides] and
[APT/Docs].

To get you started, there is a "dummy" user account that you can access
when you first start ApTline up. - Enter SYSOP as your name and use APTBBS
when requested to enter a password. - You should change this password to
something else before you put the BBS online to other users!

Note: That if you start line 0 up the supplied script will auto-load in the
test account of "Sysop". But for any other BBS line number you will need to
enter your name and password. You can of course alter the LOGON.APT script
to suit your requirements at a suitable date.

